{
  "why_fit": "Epidarex Capital’s investment in HydroNTech (anion-exchange membrane electrolysers for green hydrogen) demonstrates a clear appetite for UK-based climate hardware with strong technical defensibility. Thermafold’s designed-for-Britain air-source heat pump using R290 propane (low global warming potential) and targeting a seasonal coefficient of performance of 3.5 meets their thesis of funding “high-impact, technically difficult problems” in climate tech and frontier hardware. Founded by a chartered mechanical engineer with 12 years at Mitsubishi Electric UK’s heat pump division, the team brings deep domain expertise. Although Epidarex often backs university spin-outs, they also back experienced founders; Thermafold’s planned pilot with a housing association and clear path to MCS certification provide the regulatory and revenue milestones they look for. The £2.5M seed round fits squarely within their typical £500k–£4M cheque range. The main gap is that Thermafold has not yet filed patents, whereas Epidarex usually seeks strong intellectual property defensibility — this should be addressed in conversations.",
  "how_to_pitch": "Lead with the engineering pedigree and the structural UK demand for heat pumps (government net-zero targets, Boiler Upgrade Scheme). Cite the housing association pilot as a de-risking milestone. Emphasise the R290 design choices that improve efficiency and reduce environmental impact — position this as the core technical moat, but be ready to discuss any patent filings or trade secrets. Reference HydroNTech as a portfolio parallel to show you understand their climate hardware focus. Stress that your target unit cost (£1,800) and UK-specific design (MCS compliance, hot water tank integration) solve a real market gap. Avoid overplaying US expansion plans — keep the pitch centred on UK deployment and MCS certification. Ask for an introduction to the climate tech lead partner (likely Sinclair Dunlop) and frame the ask around a lead or co-lead seed cheque of £1.5–2M. Prepare to discuss follow-on reserved capital (1.5–2x) and how you will reach £5M+ annual recurring revenue within three to five years via housing associations and retrofitters.",
  "drafted_email_subject": "Thermafold – UK-designed heat pump hardware seeking £2.5M seed round",
  "drafted_email_body": "Dear Sinclair,\n\nI’m writing to introduce Thermafold — a UK hardware startup designing residential air-source heat pumps optimised for British semi-detached homes. We use R290 propane refrigerant (low GWP) and target a seasonal COP of 3.5, with an OEM unit cost under £1,800. We have two working prototypes and a housing association pilot lined up for Q3 2026, pending MCS certification.\n\nI founded Thermafold after 12 years as a chartered mechanical engineer at Mitsubishi Electric UK’s heat pump division, so I understand the incumbent’s weaknesses and the UK installer ecosystem intimately.\n\nWe are raising a £2.5M seed round at an £8M pre-money valuation. Your investment in HydroNTech shows you back UK climate hardware with real technical differentiation, so I believe there’s a strong fit with your thesis.\n\nI’d welcome the chance to walk you through our engineering data, pilot plan, and unit economics. Are you available for a brief call next week?\n\nBest,\n[Founder name]\n[Phone/email]",
  "source_citations": [
    {
      "type": "fund_decision",
      "text": "Epidarex Capital led a £2.2M seed round in Microbinder (UCL spinout) in June 2025, demonstrating their active seed-stage cheque size within the £500k–£4M range.",
      "source": "Investor profile: Recent activity"
    },
    {
      "type": "partner_statement",
      "text": "Epidarex states they 'back founders solving high-impact, technically difficult problems in … climate tech, and frontier hardware'.",
      "source": "Investor profile: Thesis"
    },
    {
      "type": "portfolio_precedent",
      "text": "Epidarex co-led a £3.5M Series A in HydroNTech, a UK-based electrolyser hardware company developing anion-exchange membrane technology for green hydrogen — a direct parallel to Thermafold’s climate hardware focus.",
      "source": "Investor profile: Recent activity and Notable portfolio"
    }
  ]
}
